  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its siting, design and level of illuminance, would result in an unnecessary and harmful addition to street clutter within this section of the public footway. The cumulative impact of these features would detract from the established character of the Kingsley Road and diminish the quality of the public realm. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policy D8 (Public Realm), Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures), and the aims of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its excessive scale, siting and design would result in an unacceptable level of obstruction to vehicle users and pedestrian visibility and would adversely affect highway and pedestrian safety. The development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) and Policy CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures)."
  ],
